IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 1 April 2022 -- LAYER 1: THE NOUNS.  Facts a witness of ordinary competence could give about a
-- contract, a guarantee, some property and a remedy.  No rule is stated here; every rule is in
-- mca-act.l4, and the questions a person asks are in mca-seat.l4.
--
-- Terms the Act does not define are not defined here either.  "Minor" in particular is not defined by this
-- Act (and the age of majority is in no source we have), so whether a party was a minor when the
-- contract was made is a FACT the person states; no age is typed anywhere in this row.  The same goes for
-- "unenforceable", "repudiates", "guarantee", "obligation", "property" and "the court".

§ `The nouns -- a contract with a minor`

-- One contract is the Act's natural unit.  "He" in ss 2(b) and 3(1)(b) is the party who was a minor
-- (the principal debtor under s 2, the defendant under s 3).
DECLARE `Contract with a minor` HAS
    `day the contract was made` IS A DATE                                                    -- ss 1, 2(a), 3(1)(a), 4: the date bands
    `one party was a minor when the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN                          -- s 1 "made by a minor"; ss 2(b), 3(1)(b) "because he was a minor" (read first: no minor, no "because")
    `the obligation is unenforceable against that party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN                  -- ss 2(b), 3(1)(b), first limb (the Act's premise, law outside the sources: asked, never decided here; NOTHING = not known)
    `that party repudiates the contract` IS A BOOLEAN                                        -- ss 2(b), 3(1)(b), the parenthesis
    `that is because that party was a minor when the contract was made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN   -- ss 2(b), 3(1)(b) "because he was a minor ..."; see fork F1 in NOTES.md; NOTHING = not known
    `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the provision applicable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN   -- s 4 exception: a borrowed legal fact (that Act is not among the sources); NOTHING = not known

§ `The nouns -- a guarantee (section 2)`

DECLARE `Guarantee case` HAS
    `the contract guaranteed` IS A `Contract with a minor`
    `a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(a)

§ `The nouns -- restitution (section 3)`

DECLARE `Restitution case` HAS
    `the contract sued on` IS A `Contract with a minor`
    `the claimant entered into the contract with the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN                    -- s 3(1)(a): the claimant is a person who has entered into a contract with another

DECLARE Property HAS
    `acquired by the defendant under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- s 3(1) "any property acquired by the defendant under the contract"
    `represents property acquired by the defendant under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN             -- s 3(1) "or any property representing it"

DECLARE Transferee IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `someone other than the claimant`

DECLARE Remedy HAS
    `other than a transfer under section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(2) "any other remedy"
    `available to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN                  -- s 3(2) "available to the claimant"

-- The two people s 3 names, and the one official who acts; used by the court's permission in s 3(1).
DECLARE `Party under section 3` IS ONE OF
    `the court`
    `the claimant`
    `the defendant`

DECLARE `Act under section 3` IS ONE OF
    `require the defendant to transfer property to the claimant`

§ `The nouns -- the Act's own defined terms (section 3(1)(a))`

-- The Act defines two words, both by a label in a bracket: "(the claimant)" and "(the defendant)".
DECLARE `Defined term in the Act` HAS
    term IS A STRING
    `where defined` IS A STRING
    `the Act's words` IS A STRING
    `plain gloss` IS A STRING
